Z||000000||Lynx||06-23-99||01:06 AM||||First i have a 85 2m4 with a five speed. Well i hear all these people saying that there 4 cylinder is gettin 33-35 mpg on the highway. Well mine only gets like 25-27 on the highway and like 20-23 in town. I know they get way better on the highway than in town but mine dosent. I have new plugs,wires,cap,rotor,and air filter. So those cant be it. The Engine seems to run great even better than most 4 cylinders, juts the bad gas. The car has 200,000 but the guy i bought it from said some stuff was done to the engine by the guy who had it before him. I totally belive that because it doesnt smoke and uses NO oil. Just the damn gas mileage. Please any suggestions, the gas prices here on the west coast are OUTRAGOUS.<p>Lynx<p>P.S. I only use supreme 92octane fuel.
Z||000001||Hock||06-23-99||12:02 PM||||First stop using 92 octane. That itself can hurt fuel mileage. The highest grade is not always the best grade. I did the same thing with my Bronco II and it got worse fuel mileage than what it did with 89. Second, how do you drive your Fiero. Do you excelerate hard all the time? That itself can drasticly reduce your fuel mileage. Also what type of tires do you run? Wide tires can also hurt fuel mileage. So that is everything I know to check. Good Luck! 
Z||000002||batboy||06-23-99||12:59 PM||||The amount of air pressure in your tires can affect gas mileage too. My 4 cylinder, 1987 Fiero usually gets 32 to 35 mpg on the highway when I drive approximately 55 to 60 mph. If I drive faster, like 70 to 75 mph on the interstate, or if I have the A/C on, I get far less. My fuel mileage also drops in the winter months.
Z||000003||DJRice||06-23-99||03:41 PM||||Did you get any specifics on what mods if any were done to the engine?  I had a friend who rebuilt the 2.5L 4cyl in his Ford Ranger who managed to find a "radical high end cam" for it.  Basically the thing sounded like a strung out VW when it was finished. It did run good, although not tremendously faster, but burned more gas than before.  If the person who had it before you added some crazy performance parts to it than you may be doing the best you can do.<p>Does the exhaust smell rich, have you had the TBI checked to see if it needs to be adjusted.  This could get pricey, but it may help narrow down your problem.
Z||000004||Lynx||06-23-99||06:39 PM||||First i do drive about 70-75 mph on the Freeway. Never 55 or 65. I dont have the A/C on it guzzles gas then. Well i dont know if there was any mods done to it. It runs smooth like a stock cam so i dont think anything was done to it. It does seem to have more power than most Fiero 2.5's ( I can WASTE Miata'a). There is no check enegine light so i dont think its runnin rich. Thanks for the suggestions so far.
Z||000005||Yellow85||06-23-99||07:17 PM||||I have question for V6 owners.<br>I have 85 V6 with 4spd and 215/60/14 tires.<br>I drive 70-75 on high-way and almost no mod on my engine. my car has 10 galons tank. it only can run 300-350km per tank. Is this normal?  I heard other V6 owners` milage are better than mine,but i thought it because of 4spd trans. 
Z||000006||SCCA FIERO||06-23-99||09:49 PM||||I have an 86SE V6 with the 4 speed and I get only 180 miles out of a tank. How does that convert to Km?As far as I know it has not been modified,but it runs very strong.
Z||000007||theogre||06-23-99||10:09 PM||||Did you check the ECM to make sure there are no codes in it? If the motor is running "open loop" and you don't know it then you'll drink more gas. With the 2.5l the Open loop mode runs almost identically to it's normal mode to most people. (If the ECM lamp is not lit when cranking, or the key is on, then it's lamp may be bad or removed.)<p>You can get a "code reader" fer a few dollars. it just plugs into the ALDL connector and has it's own lamp. All these do is read codes.<p>The alternate, which I strongly recomend to anyone doing there own repairs, is the AutoXray GM scanner. This will not only get codes, but let you test sensors as well. For example, if the Throtle Position sensor is changing value, and you aren't pusshing the pedal, you got a problem.
Z||000008||Yellow85||06-24-99||01:18 AM||||SCCA FIERO,<br>is it on high-way?  if it is.....then my GT is even better gas than your`s. 
Z||000009||lowCG||06-24-99||03:14 AM||||You might be able to "optimise" by using the middle grade gas,and adjusting the timing to where it doesn't ping,yet has the best vacume/driveability.I marked the dist/block with a scratch,then started to adjust away until it ran the best.Took awhile,but<br>might get you a MPG or two.<br>Never checked my mileage,know it was over 30,just didn't step on it when I was broke.My car ran better with the best gas too,just couldn't get into spending that much $ all the time.<br>
