Z||000012||Lynx||06-25-99||01:38 AM||||Speaking of tanks, How much gas does a tank in a Fiero hold? See the guy i bought it from says to fill it at a 1/4 tank becuase it runs empty at a 1/8 of a tank but it only holds about 6 gallons from a 1/4 to full. Is the tank that small or is the guy just dumb and dosent know that the meter moves around alot?
Z||000013||Cooter||06-25-99||04:20 PM||||As far as I know the Fiero holds 10 gallons, but it is better to fill it up at about 1/4 for different reasons. THe main one is the tank mounted fuel pump is cooled by the fuel in the tank. Low fuel levels mean a hot pump, hot may mean shorter life, but may not. I just fill up at the quarter mark out of habbit.
Z||000014||theogre||06-25-99||10:42 PM||||No year of Fiero Fuel tank is less than 10 US gallon capacity. If the tank is going "empty", yet takes less than 10 gallons to fill, Huston you have a problem.<p>The problem is likely a short/bent pickup. This problem can only be corrected by dropping the tank. The solution is as annoying at least at having a 6 gallon usable capacity but you only have to fix it once.
Z||000015||SCCA FIERO||06-26-99||02:18 AM||||My 86V6 and my 88 4 cylinder both go all the way to E without running out of gas. The 86 holds 10 gallons and the 88 will take 12 gallons.<p> One thing the does bug me is the 88,when it gets full and the pump clicks it spits some out on the car.
Z||000016||Yellow85||06-26-99||03:05 AM||||Hey guys, guess what?  i was driving on high way few days ago and my car run out of gas. I had to walk a mile to get gas and i almost got hit by truck.  Make sure fill up your car above E-line when you drive on highway!! 
Z||000017||Carrolles||06-28-99||12:40 PM||||I have an 85SE with the v-6 and Muncie 4spd.  On the Daytona trip last year the best mileage I got was 28mpg at 75mph with A/C running.  I got on the highway right after filling up and filled up again when I got off the highway.  The 85 has a 10 gallon tank.  At 70 mph I'm turning 3000 rpm.<br>Usually around town at home (about 50% highway driving) I average around 22 mpg.
